# Shell scripts and SLURM batch files MUST have LF endings.
#
# This is not a style preference. RUNLOG.md section 4 records `sbatch`
# rejecting a submission script because it had CRLF line endings, and the error
# it gives does not mention line endings. The repo is edited on Windows, so
# without this every new script is born broken.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.sbatch        text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything the cluster reads as a script or config.
*.py            text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf

# Structure files are deliberately NOT normalised. Our readers slice fixed
# columns and ignore a trailing CR, every tool in the pipeline does the same,
# and normalising them would rewrite every committed PDB and CIF in data/ for
# no behavioural gain. Line endings only matter where a shell executes the
# file.

# Keep binary things binary.
*.pt            binary
*.pth           binary
*.ckpt          binary
*.npz           binary
*.png           binary
*.pdf           binary
